theorem no-least-positive
  metamath    nominpos
  note        Below any positive real x lies the positive real x/2, so no
              positive real is the least.
  then there is no x ∈ ℝ with 0 < x and there is no y ∈ ℝ with 0 < y and y < x

1.  There is no x ∈ ℝ with 0 < x and there is no y ∈ ℝ with 0 < y and y < x.
    contradiction
    suppose there is x ∈ ℝ with 0 < x and there is no y ∈ ℝ with 0 < y and y < x   (S)

    1.1.  x ∈ ℝ. 0 < x. There is no y ∈ ℝ with 0 < y and y < x.
          obtain x from S

    1.2.  0 < x/2
          inequalities, from 1.1

    1.3.  x/2 < x
          inequalities, from 1.1

    1.4.  There is y ∈ ℝ with 0 < y and y < x.
          exhibit, from 1.2, 1.3, contradicting 1.1
